Ambassador Mike Waltz
U.S. Representative to the United Nations
New York, New York
AS DELIVERED
Thank you, Mr. President. And thank you, SRSG Keita for your briefing today and for your leadership of MONUSCO.
The United States supports MONUSCO and the role it plays in advancing peace and stability in the DRC.
In that vein, we too strongly condemn the continued obstruction of MONUSCO’s operations, particularly by M23 and the Rwandan Defense Forces in North Kivu. Such actions we agree are absolutely unacceptable. They undermine MONUSCO’s mandate and they prolong the suffering of the people in the region.
We too demand M23 and RDF cease obstruction of MONUSCO immediately, which they have committed to do under the Washington and Doha processes, and will allow MONUSCO to carry out its work without interference.
The United States remains committed to the implementation of the DRC-Rwanda Peace Agreement, the Washington Accords, which President Trump is proud to have facilitated just this year. This implementation is underway, with regular meetings now of the Joint Security Coordination Mechanism and Joint Oversight Committee established by these Accords and by this Agreement.
The U.S. expects the complete and timely implementation of all elements of the Agreement to advance peace, stability, prosperity in eastern DRC and the broader Great Lakes region.
We would also like to highlight the importance of the African Union role in supporting implementation of the Peace Agreement and we call on all members to support its work.
We also want to highlight and appreciate Qatar’s ongoing mediation of negotiations between the DRC and AFC/M23 in Doha, which are critical to achieving stability in eastern DRC. We are lending our full support to bringing the Doha negotiations to a successful conclusion.
As we prepare for MONUSCO’s upcoming mandate renewal, the United States is committed to working with fellow Council members to ensure the mission’s mandate is fit for purpose and that the mission reflects the realities of the current operating environment. This will enable the mission to become more efficient, it needs to become more effective, it needs to eliminate some of the unnecessary expenses and redundancies, thereby creating better value for the contributing nations – and enabling it to better support peace, stability, and the aspirations of the people of the DRC.
Thank you.
