Ting Wu
Deputy Political Counselor
New York, New York
September 29, 2025
AS DELIVERED
Thank you, Mr. President. Several colleagues made reference to a purported genocide. The United States notes these allegations are categorically false, baseless, and fuel antisemitic hate and violence around the world. Even more disturbingly, one Member State today made an allusion to the Holocaust. The United States underscores the offensive nature of these comments, which distort history and are a disgrace to all those who perished in the Holocaust and to all of the victims of Hamas’ October 7 attack, which was itself the worst massacre of Jews since the horrors of the Holocaust. Thank you.
