AS PREPARED
While many may celebrate so-called successes gained for women over the last 30 years, one must ask what defines true success for women? Is there truly success when a country cannot answer the simple question: “What is a woman?” Should we celebrate success, when UN Women, the premier UN organization focusing on women, after all of these years, still cannot simply define a “woman”? Efforts to eradicate the reality of biological sex fundamentally attack women at their core, depriving them of their uniqueness, dignity, safety, and well-being. Biological reality is rooted in scientific truth and is confirmed by the universal truths that we are endowed by our Creator who made us “male and female.” The Trump Administration is restoring and reaffirming the truth of biological reality and is ardently standing up for women, for families, and for the values that make America stronger than ever.
Sadly, birth rates are plummeting in many areas around the world including the United States. The family unit is in crisis and is being erased. The United States understands the vital role the family plays in a child’s life and development. President Trump believes that parents, both mothers and fathers, not governments, know how to best raise their children and create a thriving society. As Vice President Vance has said, “We actually think that God made male and female for a purpose. We want you to thrive as young men and as young women.” The dilution of the value held uniquely by men and women, has led to the rapid erosion of parental rights throughout our institutions. Mothers and fathers should ultimately hold the responsibility of deciding what their children are being taught, and the concept of comprehensive sexual education (CSE), is an utter violation of parental rights.
We know that we must protect and uplift women, but at the same time, we cannot beat down men in the process. Both women and men are equally
important. The Trump Administration is committed to supporting families, promoting women’s health, and protecting children at all stages of life, beginning at conception, reaffirming that there is no international right to abortion.
As we celebrate mothers, the United States also sees the great value of fathers. We want all communities and countries to flourish, which is only possible through strong families, including both mothers and fathers. How is this possible, when many countries fail to uphold the biological reality of what is female?
So, as we look forward together on how better to support and uplift women, the United States urges you to join us in our endeavor to protect women and girls from the insanity that has spread like a disease around the world: gender ideology. Men and boys are male. Women and girls are female. It’s that simple. Will you join us?
