Ambassador Jeff Bartos was nominated by the President to serve as the U.S. Representative for U.N. Management and Reform and confirmed by the U.S. Senate for this role on September 18, 2025. In this role, he is expected to focus on promoting transparency, accountability, and effective management within the United Nations system.
Mr. Bartos is a Pennsylvania-based businessman, attorney, and civic leader with extensive experience in the private sector, philanthropy, and politics. A graduate of Emory University and the University of Virginia School of Law, Bartos began his career practicing law before moving into real estate and management. He has served as president of ESB Holdings LLC and previously held senior executive roles with Mark Group, Inc. and Toll Brothers, Inc.
Mr. Bartos is well known for his leadership in community and philanthropic initiatives. During the COVID-19 pandemic, he co-founded the Pennsylvania 30 Day Fund, a nonprofit that provided forgivable loans to over 1,000 small businesses across the state, helping to preserve thousands of jobs. He also played a role in launching the Barstool Fund, which raised millions to support small businesses nationwide. Bartos has served on the boards of several nonprofits. Politically, Bartos has been active in Pennsylvania’s Republican Party and was the GOP nominee for Lieutenant Governor in 2018 and ran for the U.S. Senate in 2022. Throughout his career, he has been a vocal advocate for small businesses, economic growth, and community development.
A lifelong Pennsylvanian, Mr. Bartos and his wife Sheryl live in Montgomery County, Pennsylvania where they raised their two daughters.
